{"id": "section-body-07560", "title": "Laryngeal Diphtheria", "chapterId": "chapter-nine", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "RESPIRATORY DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Other Respiratory Infections", "Laryngeal Diphtheria"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-07560", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Laryngeal Diphtheria", "runs": [{"text": "Laryngeal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diphtheria"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1603"}}, {"id": "body-07561", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Is an infection caused by Corynebacterium diphtheria; it is directly transmitted from person to person by droplets. Children between 1–5 years of age are most susceptible although non-immune adults are also at risk. Diphtheria is characterized by grayish-white membrane, composed of dead cells, fibrin, leucocytes and red blood cells as a result of inflammation due to multiplying bacteria.", "runs": [{"text": "Is an infection caused by "}, {"text": "Corynebacterium diphtheria", "italic": true}, {"text": "; it is directly transmitted from person to person by droplets. Children between 1–5 years of age are most susceptible although non-immune adults are also at risk. Diphtheria is characterized by grayish-white membrane, composed of dead cells, fibrin, leucocytes and red blood cells as a result of inflammation due to multiplying bacteria."}]}, {"id": "body-07564", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-07565", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Isolate the child", "runs": [{"text": "Isolate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "child"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1596"}}, {"id": "body-07566", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Gently examine the child’s throat – can cause airway obstruction if 